namespace pdg { /**

\fn pdg::TimerManager::getMilliseconds

\brief get the current time in milliseconds

Returns elapsed milliseconds from a monotonic clock, with zero established at the first call in this process. System wall-clock adjustments do not affect this value. Use it for elapsed times and timer deadlines, not calendar dates. The native timestamp uses a signed 64-bit integer.

\note Many events and callbacks pass this value (or a ms delta since the last call), so you can often avoid repeated calls to getMilliseconds() by using the value or millisecond delta passed in.

**/ }